  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...A brief period of dangerous heat tomorrow, with\nvery warm, but less humid conditions Wednesday.\n\nLarge dome of high pressure will continue to expand into the \nGreat Lakes region tonight and tomorrow. Low level thicknesses\nwill build as 850mb temps rise into the the 22C-25C range (99th\npercentile for mid July) by tomorrow. This will support highs \nreaching the mid to even upper 90s across the Lake Plains,\nGenesee Valley and Finger Lakes, and upper 80s to lower 90s \nelsewhere.\n\nWinds will strengthen as well tomorrow under a strong LLJ, with \n25-40 mph gusts possible, which will also advect in a plume of \nhigher moisture with Tds reaching the low 70s across the lower \nelevations. As a result, heat indices will climb into the lower \n100s here, and even as high as 105 degrees. Elsewhere, peak heat\nindices will reach the mid to upper 90s. A Heat Advisory \ncontinues for all of WNY from 11 am to 8 pm tomorrow.\n\nVery warm and humid conditions will remain into at least the first \npart of Wednesday, before an approaching mid level trough and \nsurface cold front drop south out of eastern Canada ushering in \ncooler and drier air from north to south through the second half of \nthe day. High temps will still range through the 80s by early \nWednesday afternoon, but dropping humidity levels will keep heat \nindices about the same as the actual air temperature.",
